<title>USA: Kansas feedlot cattle quiet, no trade - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas feedlot cattle quiet, no trade - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade was quiet, with no sales slaughter steers or heifers confirmed, USDA said.</p>
<p>Inquiry was moderate, demand light. Sales confirmed for the week to date on 1,200 cattle, mostly previously contracted or formulated cattle. Tuesday's bids $65.00-$66.00 per cwt, asking $67.00-$68.00. Sales FOB feedlot net weights after 4 percent shrink. Confirmed - none.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
</text>
